5. Cell Expansion: separate a repeated lattice into identifiable unit cells.
6. Packing View: display the atom arrangement with an appropriate packing representation.
7. Comparison Mode: compare two structures using consistent scale conventions.
8. Camera Reset: restore a useful default viewing angle.

Do not fake an exploded view by simply enlarging the entire structure. The selected cell or repeated unit cells must visibly separate in a controlled and reversible manner.

D. Parameter Panel

Include scientifically useful parameters such as:

